1. <seg id="s0002" group="l0001" targets="p1" role="patient_specific">Case presentation
The patient is a 33-year-old Caucasian woman
who presented to the University of Washington in
March of 1994. She had a 2-year history of type 1
diabetes complicated by numerous episodes of
diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) requiring hospital-
ization. During the previous 9 months, a 9-kg
weight loss accompanied symptoms of uncon-
trolled hyperglycemia. Her insulin dose was 60 U
per day of human insulin, split into two injections</seg>
